# dag-unix-test-baseline-compat.patch
#
# Additive compatibility patch for an ISOLATED Unix snapshot only. Not applied to the shared
# working tree, and it does not claim the current tree builds on Unix.
#
# Source of truth: /tmp/ferryx-dag-unix-first-spawn.log (66 errors). All 31 E0063 sites were
# re-located by file:line from that log, so this covers exactly the logged failure set.
#
#   E0063 x31  DaemonResponse::HandshakeOk literals missing `capabilities` and
#              `admission_time_unix_ms`
#                src/daemon/client.rs                 11
#                src/ipc/tests.rs                      17
#                src/remote/tests.rs                    2
#                src/ipc/agents_reset_event_tests.rs     1
#   E0277 x5   ValidatedFile (src/ipc/remote_drop.rs:79) needs Debug for the drop tests
#              -> #[derive(Debug)] (fields are String/String/u64; the derive is inert)
#
# Semantics of the two added fields, mirroring the production handshake
# (src-tauri/src/daemon/server.rs:2835-2844):
#   capabilities           -> vec![LOCAL_SPLIT_LIFECYCLE_CAPABILITY]; that is the only
#                             capability the daemon advertises, and the client's
#                             require_capability gate (daemon/client.rs:961-968) checks
#                             exactly this capability plus a present admission time.
#   admission_time_unix_ms -> Some(current unix ms), the same observed value
#                             AdmissionClock::now() yields on first use
#                             (daemon/session_service.rs:146-153).
#   Why defaults are safe: all 31 literals live in #[cfg(all(test, unix))] modules that have
#   not compiled since the local-split feature landed, so none of them can encode an
#   "incapable daemon" expectation. The single test that asserts UnsupportedCapability builds
#   its peer reply from JSON with accept(false) (daemon/client.rs:3911-3915; assertion at
#   :3977), so this patch does not touch it.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED:
#   * src/terminal/shell.rs HRTB closure + src/terminal/pty.rs comparisons -> reuse
#     scripts/qa/dag-test-baseline-compat.patch + scripts/qa/dag-pty-test-baseline-compat.patch
#   * src/daemon/session_service.rs spawn-command shape -> scripts/qa/dag-baseline-compat.patch
#   * src/ssh/operations.rs E0425/E0433 (upload_deadline_for_bytes, Duration,
#     posix_drop_upload_script, windows_drop_upload_script): production in-flight work that
#     needs its owner's semantic decision, not a compat default. BLOCKED here.
#   * E0282/E0283 at src/remote/machine_agent_state_tests.rs:261,315: already fixed in the
#     current tree (Ok::<AgentState, anyhow::Error>), so no hunk is emitted.
#   * "couldn't read" errors for scripts/install.sh, scripts/install.ps1,
#     docs/evidence/paired-daemon/fixtures/*.json, scripts/qa/daas-project-response.json:
#     those files exist in the current tree and are missing from the snapshot. Include them
#     when building the snapshot; a patch cannot add files that already exist here.
#
# Verify + apply (repo root, isolated snapshot):
#   git apply --check -p1 scripts/qa/dag-unix-test-baseline-compat.patch
#   git apply -p1 scripts/qa/dag-unix-test-baseline-compat.patch
#
# Additive only: no suppressions, no #[ignore]/#[cfg] additions, no removals, no production
# behavior change (the derive is inert; every handshake field added is a test fixture value).
